          "literatureReview": "24-hour urine metanephrine measures O-methylated catecholamine metabolites. Normal: metanephrine <350 µg/24h, normetanephrine <600 µg/24h. Elevated in pheochromocytoma, paraganglioma, and neuroblastoma. More sensitive than plasma metanephrines. Requires 24-hour collection with acid preservative. HPLC with electrochemical detection provides accurate quantification. Used for adrenal tumor diagnosis and monitoring. Critical for catecholamine-secreting tumor detection."
